Today was a great day. One of the best in awhile.
I turned 30 today and while I joke about being old or whatever, it feels good and I'm thankful for it.
Lots of people reached out to me on Facebook and I actually replied to them this year.
The day started off good. I woke up, got some coffee, and hopped on the laptop to 'work'. Luckily on Fridays, I can work from home.
I usually do work as I normally would but since it's my birthday and I've been going kinda hard on work recently, I decided to take it real easy.
Brittany made me some chocolate chip pancakes for breakfast and it was delicious. I love her so much and she brings me so much joy.
After work, we checked on the cats, George and Twinks (or Twinx?). After that, instead of making burritos, we went to Burgatory which was unusually good this time. The server from the car and he was real cool. We told him we were vegan and he asked if it was okay if the grill was shared with meat. A consideration that we never expect but it awesome when someone does. My burger was great and Brittany said hers was really good too! Better than usual.
After Burgatory, we had enough time to go to the mall and we went to Macy's. We sniffed a bunch of colognes and found a really good one from Dior that has a basic cologne smell, but with a crisp lemony and citrus aftersmell. I immediately knew that was the one I wanted and Brittany bought it for me! I love the smell and the guy there was real nice, he also gave Brittany a lil sample perfume.
Then it was time to go to the movies to see Superman and wow, what an amazing movie. It's not often that I see a movie and want to watch the New Rockstars breakdown (which are usually 1hr+ long videos), but this was one of those movies. The acting, action, cinematography, comedy, emotion, and storyteling were all great. I loved that movie and I love that I got to watch it with Brittany. There was a little debacle with someone taking our seat originally and some noisy old folks next to us, but other than that, it's the best time I've had at the movies in a long time.
After getting home and getting to smooch and hold Brittany for a bit, I played some WoW and watched the New Rockstars breakdown on Superman.
Overall just an amazing day and I'm so thankful that it turned out like this. I've been spending so much time working and not enough time actually enjoying life. Work is important, but actually enjoying day to day life is so much more important. Sometimes I lose sight of that and it's nice to have these days that pull me back into enjoyment and fufillment.
Going back to the morning, I spend most of it blairing a music playlist that I made on the spot and singing along. This is what I'm talking about. Instead of mindless grinding Bootdev or some work project, I enjoyed myself.
Today, I sang, watched movies, and enjoyed some delicious food. That's what it's all about.
